          "turn_index": 1,
          "type": "turn",
          "question": "How often should it be checked?",
          "answer": "The frequency of checking blood pressure can depend on whether you have been diagnosed with hypertension or other health conditions. For individuals without high blood pressure, regular monitoring during routine check-ups may be sufficient.\n\nIf you have been diagnosed with hypertension, more frequent monitoring is usually recommended. It is often advised to check blood pressure at least once a week at home, especially if you are managing your condition with lifestyle changes or medications (source: Hypertension guidelines).\n\nFor those starting blood pressure medications or adjusting treatments, your doctor may recommend more frequent measurements. The exact schedule should be tailored to your personal health needs and should be discussed with your healthcare provider (source: Major cardiology society consensus guidance).\n\nIf you have any concerns about your blood pressure or how often it should be checked, please talk to your healthcare provider for personalized advice.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
